Local partial backport: acknowledge AP-to-BGF CCIF channels during MT6897
power-on, after clearing firmware-own interrupts and before releasing the
BGF CPU. This restores the vendor startup acknowledgment sequence.

Local adaptation: report acknowledgment submission at INFO level; retain
the existing register helper and its mapping-failure diagnostics.

Link: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_modules_and_devicetree_oneplus_mt6897/commit/581b111f07d4368776397388737bc84312d921b7
Link: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_modules_and_devicetree_oneplus_mt6897/blob/76792af3e1fefabd34be6dd684bfc9facc4d5b17/vendor/mediatek/kernel_modules/connectivity/bt/mt66xx/include/btif/platform_6897.h#L1355
Signed-off-by: Dian QK <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
--- a/connectivity/bt/mt66xx/include/btif/platform_6897.h
+++ b/connectivity/bt/mt66xx/include/btif/platform_6897.h
@@ -143,6 +143,8 @@
 
 #define BGF_MCCR_SET					(BGF_REG_BASE_ADDR + 0x0104)
 #define BGF_CON_CR_AHB_STOP				BIT(2)
+
+#define BGF2AP_CONN_INFRA_ON_CCIF4_BGF2AP_PCCIF_ACK_ADDR (0x1803E014)
 
 #define BGF_SW_IRQ_RESET_ADDR				(0x1803F014)
 #define BGF_SW_IRQ_STATUS				(0x1803F010)
@@ -1364,6 +1366,12 @@
 	BTMTK_DBG("clear fw own IRQ");
 	REG_WRITEL(BGF_IRQ_STAT, BGF_IRQ_FW_OWN_SET_B);
 	REG_WRITEL(BGF_IRQ_STAT2, BGF_IRQ_FW_OWN_SET_B);
+
+	/* Acknowledge AP-to-BGF CCIF before releasing the CPU. */
+	BTMTK_INFO("BGF startup: submit CCIF4 ACK addr=0x%08x value=0xff",
+		   BGF2AP_CONN_INFRA_ON_CCIF4_BGF2AP_PCCIF_ACK_ADDR);
+	bt_write_cr(BGF2AP_CONN_INFRA_ON_CCIF4_BGF2AP_PCCIF_ACK_ADDR,
+		    0xFF, FALSE);
 
 	/* release n10 cpu core */
 	SET_BIT(CONN_INFRA_RGU_BGFSYS_CPU_SW_RST, BGF_CPU_SW_RST_B);
